1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,212
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:04,295 --> 00:00:05,296
[CALOY] <i>'Bi?</i>

3
00:00:05,797 --> 00:00:07,173
[BEA] <i>I'll wait for you outside.</i>

4
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,092
[SHARP STAB]

5
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:10,844
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [COP GROANING]

6
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:14,556
[CALOY]<i> I knew you couldn't</i>
<i>stay away from me.</i>

7
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:17,100
<i>We have a lot of work to do.</i>

8
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:21,396
- [JUDE] <i>Cake. Cake.</i>
- [BILLY] <i>Just one slice.</i>

9
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:28,737
<i>You again?!</i>
<i>I told you not to come back!</i>

10
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,947
<i>Calm down. It's not him.</i>

11
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:33,324
[JORDAN]
<i>This was supposed to be just for you.</i>

12
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:36,327
[BILLY] <i>Ever since we were kids, we've</i>
<i>always celebrated our birthdays together.</i>

13
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:38,455
<i>So it can't be just about me!</i>

14
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:40,832
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

15
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:41,875
<i>To me!</i>

16
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:45,628
- [JORDAN] <i>This is your birthday gift.</i>
<i>- Wow! You're so sweet.</i>

17
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:46,838
<i>Open it.</i>

18
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,381
<i>No way.</i>

19
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:51,551
[JORDAN SINGING]
<i>♪ When you come home ♪</i>

20
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,804
<i>♪ Weighed down and broken ♪</i>

21
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:56,473
<i>♪ I can tell ♪</i>

22
00:00:57,223 --> 00:01:01,770
<i>♪ By the words unspoken ♪</i>

23
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:07,442
<i>♪ So come here by my side ♪</i>

24
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:13,198
<i>♪ Let's leave the rest</i>
<i>Of the world aside ♪</i>

25
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:18,495
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

26
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:21,247
[ENRICO] <i>I'll never get tired of asking</i>
<i>for your forgiveness, Billy.</i>

27
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:26,294
<i>I understand why you can't</i>
<i>forgive me right away.</i>

28
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:29,005
<i>I should've been the one</i>
<i>you could lean on.</i>

29
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:31,007
<i>But I wasn't there for you.</i>

30
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:32,967
<i>Either of you.</i>

31
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:35,303
<i>I just hope you'll give me another chance.</i>

32
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:38,139
<i>Happy birthday, my Billy.</i>

33
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,225
<i>I'm very proud of you.</i>

34
00:01:40,308 --> 00:01:45,647
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

35
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:48,399
<i>♪ Let's leave the rest</i>
<i>Of the world aside ♪</i>

36
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:51,528
<i>♪ With all its baggage ♪</i>

37
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:53,696
<i>♪ Whatever happens ♪</i>

38
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,782
<i>♪ Lean on me ♪</i>

39
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:59,077
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

40
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,538
<i>♪ Lean on me ♪</i>

41
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:05,166
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

42
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:07,627
- [CHEERING, APPLAUDING]
<i>- Okay.</i>

43
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,712
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

44
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,923
<i>- Thank you.</i>
- [FRIENDS] <i>That was great!</i>

45
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:14,926
[APPLAUDING]

46
00:02:19,597 --> 00:02:22,517
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

47
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,018
- [CLEARS THROAT]
- [ENGINE CRANKS]

48
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:25,728
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]
- [CLEARS THROAT]

49
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:27,939
What?

50
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:30,150
- Yes?
- Billy.

51
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,402
Can you even drive right now?

52
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,444
Of course!

53
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:35,071
- I'm fine. Mm-mm.
- [JORDAN] You sure?

54
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,406
Yeah, absolutely.

55
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:38,366
- Thanks for your concern.
- Okay.

56
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:40,702
[BILLY] And thanks
for performing that song earlier.

57
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:41,995
- Of course.
- It was beautiful.

58
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:44,455
- [SINGING] <i>♪ Lean on me ♪</i>
- [SEATBELT CLICKS]

59
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:47,500
<i>- ♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>
<i>- ♪ Lean on me ♪</i>

60
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:49,627
[BOTH SINGING]
<i>♪ Lean on me ♪</i>

61
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:51,963
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

62
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:53,840
- It was beautiful.
- You know, let's duet sometime.

63
00:02:53,923 --> 00:02:55,049
No way!

64
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:58,052
You can make me your partner
in everything else, just not in singing.

65
00:02:58,136 --> 00:02:58,970
- Okay?
- Please?

66
00:02:59,053 --> 00:02:59,888
No!

67
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:01,180
- Okay?
- Dude, come on!

68
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:03,224
Ugh! I have to go, Jordan.

69
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:04,642
- [JORDAN CHUCKLES]
- Happy birthday!

70
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,185
- Happy birthday too.
- Happy birthday!

71
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:07,770
- You're the best! Goodbye!
- Take care.

72
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:11,858
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:03:11,941 --> 00:03:13,401
Everything's all set.

74
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:14,319
I'm ready.

75
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:15,862
I'm on my way to Billy's.

76
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,115
Caloy…

77
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:21,159
Be careful, okay?

78
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:24,454
Especially since you're still wanted.

79
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:27,999
[BEA] <i>There are cops</i>
<i>right outside the house.</i>

80
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:30,293
They're keeping watch.

81
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:33,671
Probably because they believe
we're connected.

82
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:35,215
Don't worry.

83
00:03:36,174 --> 00:03:37,634
You won't get dragged into this.

84
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:39,135
I'll make it up to you, okay?

85
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:41,554
I love you.

86
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:45,016
Um…

87
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:47,852
Love you too.

88
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:54,776
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

89
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:04,953
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

90
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:43,283
[ROBBIE] You're seriously amazing, boss!

91
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,118
That song was so good. Listen--

92
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:47,495
[SINGING]
<i>♪ Lay your head on me ♪</i>

93
00:04:47,578 --> 00:04:48,746
<i>♪ Just lay your head-- ♪</i>

94
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,248
♪ <i>Lean on me ♪</i>

95
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:52,208
Oh, were the lyrics "Lean on me"?

96
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,751
- [CHUCKLES] You're wrong!
- Sorry.

97
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:55,169
<i>♪ Lean on me ♪</i>

98
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:57,338
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

99
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:59,299
- [RAIN] There you go.
- [LAUGHS]

100
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,551
But seriously…

101
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:04,387
Is that really a friendship song?

102
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,557
Because to me, it sounds like a love song.

103
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,766
That's just you.

104
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:12,562
Then what about Billy?

105
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:14,981
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] Billy's my friend.

106
00:05:15,064 --> 00:05:16,024
Hmm?

107
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,860
It's a friendship song.

108
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:21,237
Seems more like a love song to me.
It literally says "lean on me."

109
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:22,697
Would I tell a friend to lean on me?

110
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:24,407
- No.
- That's just your perspective.

111
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:26,868
Because all you ever think about is love.

112
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:29,620
You know, Robbie still has his hopes up

113
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:32,582
because Valerie has just
broken up with Kevin.

114
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,208
I don't get him.

115
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:35,752
Good luck to you.

116
00:05:36,335 --> 00:05:37,670
Whatever.

117
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,172
But it's a love song, right?

118
00:05:39,255 --> 00:05:41,799
- He already said it's a friendship song.
- [ROBBIE] It's a love song!

119
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:44,052
Then tell me, how did it become
a friendship song?

120
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:46,721
Go, explain it to me. You can't, can you?
It's a love song.

121
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:48,347
It's friendship. I listened to the lyrics.

122
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:50,516
- I also listened to them!
- It's about friends.

123
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,643
It's also about the person
you want to lean on you.

124
00:05:52,727 --> 00:05:53,603
It could be both.

125
00:05:54,645 --> 00:05:55,938
[JORDAN] It depends on the listener.

126
00:05:56,481 --> 00:06:00,026
But personally, I wrote it for a friend.

127
00:06:00,109 --> 00:06:02,445
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

128
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:04,947
Hey. Is this true?

129
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:06,741
[JORDAN] What is it?

130
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:08,493
Caloy escaped!

131
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:10,036
What?!

132
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:14,165
[FOREBODING MUSIC BUILDS,
THEN SLOWLY FADES]

133
00:06:23,257 --> 00:06:26,260
[WATER TRICKLING]

134
00:06:28,262 --> 00:06:29,931
- Hey, Billy!
- [BILLY YELPS]

135
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:31,349
Did you see it?

136
00:06:31,432 --> 00:06:34,769
- I didn't even take it out!
- No, I didn't see anything.

137
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:37,313
[PRECIOUS] Why did you
even get thirsty at this time?

138
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:39,107
Yeah, why did I even get thirsty?

139
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:42,860
It was supposed to be a surprise.

140
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:44,153
Was it a surprise?

141
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:47,532
I didn't expect it, Auntie Pres!

142
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:50,660
Although you've been doing it
for 15 years every year.

143
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:52,703
Still, it should've been a surprise.

144
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:55,289
Thank you.

145
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:57,208
Happy birthday.

146
00:06:57,834 --> 00:06:59,043
[BILLY] Hm.

147
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:03,297
[GASPS] I'm so surprised!

148
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:05,716
- Thank you!
- You're welcome.

149
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,176
But for tomorrow…

150
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,970
- Pretend that this is the cake.
- [BILLY GASPS]

151
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:10,555
Do you want to eat it already?

152
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:12,348
- Not yet.
- Okay, we'll eat it tomorrow.

153
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,475
- I won't remember this.
- You saw nothing, right?

154
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:15,810
I didn't see anything!

155
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:22,817
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

156
00:07:25,403 --> 00:07:26,571
[LINE RINGING]

157
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:30,074
C'mon, dude. C'mon!

158
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:35,955
[LINE CONTINUES RINGING]

159
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:43,963
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC FADING]

160
00:07:53,264 --> 00:07:54,515
Good night.

161
00:08:00,938 --> 00:08:07,778
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:08:08,362 --> 00:08:09,822
[PHONE RINGING]

163
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:29,383
- [STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [SPRAY PAINT HISSING]

164
00:08:44,732 --> 00:08:49,320
- [STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [SPRAY PAINT HISSING]

165
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:51,614
- [BILLY GRUNTS]
- [BODY THUDS]

166
00:08:57,203 --> 00:09:03,668
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

167
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:17,974
[INHALES SHARPLY]
Hurry up. Hurry up.

168
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:19,600
[GRUNTS]

169
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:23,187
- Give up already!
- [YELLS] Help! Let me go!

170
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:26,524
- [GRUNTING, GROANING]
- Stop resisting!

171
00:09:26,607 --> 00:09:29,235
- Auntie Pres! Help!
- Stop it!

172
00:09:29,318 --> 00:09:30,987
Shut up-- [CALOY YELPS]

173
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:33,197
- [BILLY YELPS]
- [HEAVY THUD]

174
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:38,327
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

175
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:40,246
Auntie, was that Billy?

176
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:43,249
Stay there and lock the door.

177
00:09:53,426 --> 00:10:00,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:08,733
My God, Billy!

179
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:09,817
Billy!

180
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:10,776
Billy?

181
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:13,029
Help! Please help us!

182
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:14,405
Billy? Billy!

183
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:17,033
My God, Billy, what happened?

184
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,869
Billy! Billy. Billy?

185
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:21,537
Help!

186
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,748
Please help us!

187
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:25,875
Billy? Billy, Billy, Billy.

188
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:27,001
My God!

189
00:10:27,084 --> 00:10:28,085
Jordan!

190
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,838
Jordan, help me!

191
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:33,174
- Auntie Pres!
- Billy?

192
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:34,967
- What happened to Billy?
- Watch her for a second.

193
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,969
I'll call an ambulance.

194
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:37,887
Dude!

195
00:10:37,970 --> 00:10:38,846
[JORDAN] Billy.

196
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:40,431
Hey.

197
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:43,643
No, no, no, no, no, no.

198
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:50,066
<i>Why did you punch him?</i>
<i>You should've let it go.</i>

199
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,525
<i>They were teasing me.</i>

200
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:54,737
<i>They said I'd fail to get</i>
<i>into computer engineering.</i>

201
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:57,740
<i>Once your mother finds out about this,</i>
<i>she will be furious again.</i>

202
00:10:57,823 --> 00:10:59,533
<i>Well, I have a peace offering.</i>

203
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:03,204
<i>Wow, you even have a bribe.</i>

204
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:05,081
[LAUGHING]

205
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:06,666
<i>Look at this kid.</i>

206
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:08,000
[CHUCKLES]

207
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:14,548
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

208
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:15,841
<i>Jade?</i>

209
00:11:17,134 --> 00:11:18,427
<i>Jade!</i>

210
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:19,762
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Mommy!</i>

211
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:21,097
<i>Mommy!</i>

212
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,432
[CRYING] <i>Mommy!</i>

213
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:27,603
[SNIFFLES] <i>Mommy…</i>

214
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:34,527
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

215
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,612
[SNIFFLES] Come on, please.

216
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:41,617
[JORDAN] Billy?

217
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:45,287
Billy!

218
00:11:49,291 --> 00:11:50,376
Dude…

219
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:51,710
Hey.

220
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:54,964
I'm here.

221
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:59,176
Stay with me, okay?

222
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,177
Please.

223
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:05,933
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:10,646
[MUSIC STOPS]

225
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:24,785
- Billy?
- Dude.

226
00:12:24,869 --> 00:12:25,870
How do you feel?

227
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:27,788
I'm okay.

228
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,832
I already spoke to the doctor.

229
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:37,298
They said they didn't find any bleeding
or fractures on your scan.

230
00:12:37,381 --> 00:12:38,674
You'll be okay.

231
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:40,676
What about Oliver?

232
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:43,888
And Auntie Pres? Where are they?

233
00:12:43,971 --> 00:12:46,557
They're safe.
They just went to get some food.

234
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:48,058
Don't worry.

235
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:55,024
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:57,735
Did they catch Caloy?

237
00:12:57,818 --> 00:12:59,570
Was he the one who did this?

238
00:12:59,653 --> 00:13:01,780
[MUSIC BECOMES PENSIVE]

239
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:04,825
I caught him.
He'd already gotten to our house.

240
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:08,537
- [SPRAY PAINT HISSING]
- [BILLY GRUNTS]

241
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:11,207
<i>Hurry up.</i>

242
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:14,752
<i>- Stop resisting!</i>
<i>- Help! Let me go! </i>[GRUNTS]

243
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:16,003
[THUDS]

244
00:13:16,086 --> 00:13:21,091
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:13:21,675 --> 00:13:22,593
Hey.

246
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:28,516
I heard

247
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:31,018
he escaped from the hospital.

248
00:13:31,101 --> 00:13:34,188
I went straight to your house,
but when I got there,

249
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:36,023
you were already unconscious.

250
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:40,236
Dude, you scared the shit out of me.

251
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:43,280
Sorry.

252
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:45,741
When are they going to stop?

253
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:50,037
What they're doing to us
just keeps getting worse.

254
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:51,956
Right now,

255
00:13:52,831 --> 00:13:54,708
what matters is you're okay.

256
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:56,418
What if…?

257
00:13:56,502 --> 00:14:01,090
I just don't know what I'd do if…

258
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,510
I'm just glad you're okay.

259
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:08,222
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:11,892
- Hey.
- Billy!

261
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:13,435
Hi.

262
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:15,354
- Hey.
- [OLIVER CRYING]

263
00:14:15,437 --> 00:14:17,439
- How are you?
- Are you okay?

264
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:18,941
Yes, I'm okay.

265
00:14:19,024 --> 00:14:21,402
- Don't leave me.
- No, I'm okay now.

266
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:22,736
- Promise?
- Mm-hmm.

267
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,655
Sorry I made you worry.

268
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:26,365
[OLIVER CRYING]

269
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:27,908
[BILLY] It's okay now.

270
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:31,161
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:35,040
She fought back, so I beat her up.
I slammed her head against the wall.

272
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:36,876
For heaven's sake, Caloy!

273
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:38,210
What is wrong with you?!

274
00:14:38,294 --> 00:14:41,589
Every single one of your plans fails!
You messed up again!

275
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:44,466
Well, she thought she could outsmart me.

276
00:14:45,509 --> 00:14:48,429
My instructions were crystal clear.
Weren't they?

277
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:49,722
Why did you hurt her?

278
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:52,850
You were just supposed to spray-paint
their walls to scare her! That's it!

279
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:54,602
Why did you hurt her?

280
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:56,770
He hurt Billy?

281
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:59,189
Serves her right!

282
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:00,941
- [CALL DISCONNECTS]
- Hello?

283
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,735
[BEEPING]

284
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:06,530
Come on, 'Bi…

285
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:10,367
You were detained.

286
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:12,620
You lost your job.

287
00:15:12,703 --> 00:15:14,204
You've got a case against you.

288
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:17,541
And all of that happened because of Billy.

289
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,586
If she wants to make sure
you end up in prison,

290
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:22,004
I'm not letting that happen.

291
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:26,008
Ma, I don't want to go to prison either.

292
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:27,551
Who would?

293
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:30,930
But Caloy keeps screwing things up.

294
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:32,514
Think about it, Ma.

295
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:36,769
If one of us gets caught,

296
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:38,479
we'll all get dragged into this.

297
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:40,314
Well, if you don't want to do it,

298
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:42,232
Caloy and I will do it for you.

299
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,275
Hey, Ma.

300
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:46,111
Stay out of this.
I've already got it handled.

301
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:47,529
You don't need to get involved.

302
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:51,158
She's already ruined
every plan you had for us.

303
00:15:51,241 --> 00:15:54,411
That's why what Caloy did
was the right thing.

304
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:59,375
What's gotten into you?

305
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:01,293
Are you sick?

306
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:02,711
You're not angry at Caloy anymore?

307
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:07,341
Not as long as he doesn't take you
away from me.

308
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:11,011
That really won't happen.

309
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,930
That will never happen.

310
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:16,725
But you know,

311
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:19,853
even though Caloy messed up,

312
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:21,522
maybe it'll still work.

313
00:16:22,606 --> 00:16:26,026
Maybe it'll scare Billy enough

314
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:28,028
for her to finally leave me alone.

315
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:29,697
I hope so.

316
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:33,867
When you were detained,

317
00:16:33,951 --> 00:16:36,203
I was all alone in this house.

318
00:16:36,954 --> 00:16:39,623
It reminded me of when your sister died.

319
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:41,917
It hurt so much.

320
00:16:43,377 --> 00:16:45,671
Being left behind hurts so much.

321
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,967
That's why I promised myself

322
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:52,678
I'd never go through that again.

323
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:55,472
Never.

324
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:57,683
Especially not with you.

325
00:16:57,766 --> 00:17:03,564
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:05,566
I'll never leave you, Ma.

327
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:15,784
- [NEIGHBOR 1] Come on.
- [NEIGHBOR 2] Let's check.

328
00:17:16,618 --> 00:17:18,579
- [NEIGHBOR 1] Let's hurry.
- [NEIGHBOR 2] My goodness.

329
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:21,457
- [NEIGHBOR 1] How scary.
- [NEIGHBOR 2] My gosh.

330
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,293
[NEIGHBOR 1] Apparently, someone broke in,
and Billy fought back.

331
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:28,005
[NEIGHBOR 2] What? Oh my God,
I hope they're okay!

332
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:29,423
[ENRICO] What happened here?

333
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:31,842
[NEIGHBOR 1] Someone broke in.

334
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:33,635
The intruder even spray-painted
their walls.

335
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:37,556
How are the people who live here?
Where are they?

336
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:40,434
[NEIGHBOR 2] Billy probably
got hurt fighting back.

337
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:42,227
They took her to the hospital.

338
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:46,190
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

339
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,357
[MUSIC FADES]

340
00:17:53,489 --> 00:17:54,615
Billy.

341
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:58,410
Let the police do their job.

342
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:00,662
What can you even do right now?

343
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:04,458
LoveList is finally back on its feet.

344
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:06,376
Just focus on getting better.

345
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:10,172
You're not thinking of
getting back at them, are you?

346
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:13,550
But they've gone too far, Auntie Pres.

347
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,971
But this will never end.

348
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:21,725
If you retaliate,
they'll just retaliate again.

349
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:23,852
Think of your brother.

350
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:26,146
That's exactly why I'm worried, Auntie.

351
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,565
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:30,859
They were able to break into our house.

353
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:32,027
What's next?

354
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:35,114
I need to stop them
before Oliver gets hurt.

355
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:42,538
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

356
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:54,633
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

357
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:57,219
Nurse, which room is Benilda Cariño in?

358
00:18:57,928 --> 00:18:59,263
Okay, sir. Hold on.

359
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,682
I'll check which room she's in.

360
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:04,309
Cariño…

361
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:13,443
[STIRRING MUSIC SWELLS]

362
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,195
<i>I'm worried whoever broke in</i>
<i>might come back,</i>

363
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:16,780
<i>so I'm watching him in school.</i>

364
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:19,950
<i>You really feel more at ease</i>
<i>when your child is with you.</i>

365
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:23,579
<i>We won't have any peace</i>
<i>until that Billy leaves us alone!</i>

366
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:25,956
[BEA] <i>Let me deal with Billy.</i>

367
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:28,041
<i>I'll handle her, okay?</i>

368
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,127
<i>Sir, what's the update on Bea Mercado?</i>

369
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:33,213
<i>Bea Mercado has been under surveillance</i>
<i>since last week.</i>

370
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,674
<i>That's what you guys always say.</i>

371
00:19:35,757 --> 00:19:37,551
<i>But nothing ever happens.</i>

372
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:41,013
<i>Why can't you just</i>
<i>leave Oliver to himself?</i>

373
00:19:41,096 --> 00:19:42,347
<i>He's not a baby.</i>

374
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:44,224
<i>You just don't understand.</i>

375
00:19:44,308 --> 00:19:45,976
<i>Understand what?</i>

376
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:49,897
<i>- That you're just leading me on?</i>
<i>- It's not like that, Brandon.</i>

377
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:52,274
[BRANDON] <i>You know,</i>
<i>you just wasted my time.</i>

378
00:19:52,357 --> 00:19:55,152
<i>I just realized how important</i>
<i>she is to me.</i>

379
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:57,446
<i>- I knew it.</i>
<i>- She's like my family.</i>

380
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:59,364
<i>I'll tell the truth.</i>

381
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:03,619
[STIRRING MUSIC SWELLS]
